{"ts": "2026-11-07T01:12:01.902130Z", "run_id": "r-20261107T0111Z-eecc", "unit": "openspec:add-code-sandbox", "seq": 5, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-006", "target": "C-ed57e3cd", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The criterion is satisfied. The tracing test passed in the latest report and asserts every clause of the scenario: tsc exits 0 on tsconfig.build.json into a fresh mkdtemp directory under node_modules/.cache holding a type module package.json, the built index.js is imported, the built workerEntryUrl of pool.js is a file URL equal to the URL of worker-entry.js beside it and that file exists, the pool created with size 1 reports size 1, a run of the normalize body gives ok true with the exact normalize value, and the pool is closed and the directory removed in finally. No other code can have answered: the built pool spawns a real Worker at workerEntryUrl(import.meta.url) when no factory is given, the test passes none, tsconfig.build.json excludes test files from the build, and worker-entry.ts answers each job through runCode. The 120000 ms bound is enforced by the test script's --test-timeout=120000. The judge's insufficient_evidence came from the split of the evidence over parts of the diff, not from a gap in the code or the test.", "text_sha256": "18314fd33d364bc7abc1719c9623d09b9470ec17734b25bbc5f6c6c61018b104", "answer_sha256": "81a243c5d12122402423825c5c9baac3e027343b193a7cf62ec7b3283b3982a7", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-11-07T01:12:01.903217Z", "run_id": "r-20261107T0111Z-eecc", "unit": "openspec:add-code-sandbox", "seq": 6, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-007", "target": "F-81bb3a33", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding is waived. It rests on the judge not seeing run-code.ts and wasm.ts, which were in another part of the diff, not on anything missing from the code. Both files are in the unit head and do what task 3.5 names: wasm.ts caches one QuickJS module per memory bucket with a Wasm memory maximum of the base pages plus the bucket, run-code.ts picks the bucket with memoryBucket, calls setMemoryLimit with memoryBytes and setMaxStackSize with clampStack of maxStackBytes and the pool's stackCapBytes, and counts the UTF-8 bytes of the output against maxOutputBytes; the prelude's walker refuses nesting deeper than 64, a __proto__ key, a toJSON member and an output over the character limit. The task's test file limits-run.test.ts exists with tests for both scenarios, so the tick is earned.", "text_sha256": "aca6bb26ed6aeecf17ad7dd053ac3158034bfcfea3231e3220ef9072b9e6fdc5", "answer_sha256": "076ed5f65106a0d13ebe8e3dc505ab6b316e3cac7c7efc3b9dd90ad77b74119c", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-11-07T01:12:01.904253Z", "run_id": "r-20261107T0111Z-eecc", "unit": "openspec:add-code-sandbox", "seq": 7, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-008", "target": "F-6f5b85ff", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding is waived. It rests on the judge not seeing run-code.ts and test/support/sandbox-exit-worker.ts, which were in another part of the diff. Both are in the unit head and do what task 3.6 names: the exit worker exits the process with status 1 on its first message, exactly as test-plan.md describes; run-code.ts sets an interrupt handler that flags the deadline and reports a run that settled or is still pending after the deadline as a timeout; pool.ts arms a watchdog at timeoutMs plus graceMs on postMessage, terminates and replaces the worker and counts a respawn, replaces a worker that exits during a job at once and an idle one lazily, and turns a throwing factory into a spawn fault. The task's test files deadline.test.ts and crash.test.ts exist, and crash.test.ts references the exit worker, so the tick is earned.", "text_sha256": "b55da1adf87ccd8a48bc3dd8125cf20edafa19f392ec6558886b9d00bb85dee0", "answer_sha256": "77f64582b9e47de57e6c04727d342cc243fbd12a7caab441fbce41fa223bd3d2", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-11-07T01:12:01.905037Z", "run_id": "r-20261107T0111Z-eecc", "unit": "openspec:add-code-sandbox", "seq": 8, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-009", "target": "F-74714d28", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding is waived. It rests on the judge not seeing src/sandbox/worker-entry.ts, which was in another part of the diff. The file is in the unit head: it reads parentPort, answers each job message with the result of runCode and turns a thrown host error into a sandbox_crash reply. Task 3.8 only asks for the built-worker test, which exists, builds with tsconfig.build.json, resolves the built pool's worker entry to the existing worker-entry.js and runs the normalize body on a pool with no factory, and it passed in the latest report. The tick is earned.", "text_sha256": "c54d2dfaad4e5149990597075a0fccdb85b133e2ef6a27f7eae42a7fdfa3ee34", "answer_sha256": "1ee0382258aec5e61bdc798170e33b797a8f12fbe5c39cfc6240caadd49a8191", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
